1
00:00:00,250 --> 00:00:03,640
Six hundred light-years away, it literally rains liquid iron.

2
00:00:04,040 --> 00:00:08,180
Meet WASP-76b, a giant exoplanet locked in a permanent nightmare.

3
00:00:08,220 --> 00:00:11,480
Its day side boils at four thousand degrees Fahrenheit.

4
00:00:12,010 --> 00:00:15,200
That is hot enough to vaporize solid iron into gas.

5
00:00:16,190 --> 00:00:19,020
Pause. Where does all that airborne metal actually go?

6
00:00:19,980 --> 00:00:24,490
Violent eleven-thousand-mile-an-hour winds sweep the iron vapor into the night side.

7
00:00:24,540 --> 00:00:28,670
Temperatures plummet, instantly condensing the vapor into molten iron raindrops.

8
00:00:28,720 --> 00:00:31,870
The planet is actually inflating like a balloon from the heat.

9
00:00:33,280 --> 00:00:36,730
It is slowly bleeding its own atmosphere out into deep space.

10
00:00:37,840 --> 00:00:39,580
